    "body": "#### vim-patch:b3a4882: runtime(doc): mention getcellwidths() in setcellwidths()\r\n\r\ncloses: vim/vim#21362\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/b3a4882a915634c6031a4b4c8e25d459ac7b4319\r\n\r\n\r\n#### vim-patch:5959274: runtime(doc): Tweak documentation style\r\n\r\ncloses: vim/vim#21361\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/5959274607038bac22e9dde740060ddb748fedfe\r\n\r\nOmit :h :source-dryrun as it needs changes to port to Nvim anyway.\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Hirohito Higashi <h.east.727@gmail.com>\r\n\r\n\r\n#### vim-patch:683dabc: runtime(iar): Improve support for IAR compiler\r\n\r\n1. Error message can start from long word or the path to the file can be\r\n   long; in both of these cases the message will be moved to the next\r\n   line:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"/tmp/test_test_test_test_test_test_test_test_test.c\",3  Error[Pe077]:\r\n          this declaration has no storage class or type specifier\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo handle this `errorformat` will consider leading space as part of the\r\nerror message.\r\n\r\n2. Some of the messages have `[note]:` prefix.\r\n\r\n3. When messages come one after another, `%Z` is required to separate\r\n   them.\r\n\r\ncloses: vim/vim#21360\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/683dabcb916e4004be283377b8a1a0c6476598fc\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Andrey Starodoubtsev <andrey.starodoubtsev@gehealthcare.com>",
